Blind classes, made from /home/agent2/prior/pairs.md alone, before opening anything else.
(Study dates are not in pairs.md; where "dated before my study" matters I say so.)

W1  found in part  Kadir-Fan state weak tile = tile only for Z_pq, a narrower class than p^n q / pqr / p^2 q^2 (and only if July 2026 is before the study); the other two passages concern other groups or conditions.
W2  not found      "One of the strongest bonds" is neither optimality, nor among bonds without straight joints, nor by a stated measure of cost; it asserts something weaker than the claim.
W3  found          Abdelgalil's passages state the count is finite and odd and can be 3, 5, 7 or more; no number in the claim (caveat: the passages show a perturbative setting, epsilon, which may be a narrower class).
W4  found          Helbing et al. state direct ways first, then shared trails, ending in a "minimal way system"; no number in the claim (the word Y and "three points" are not in the quoted passages).
W5  found in part  Earlier flowering in Germany and the tie to temperature are stated, but no snowdrop figure near 10 days (coltsfoot "nearly a week" is another species and outside 8.5-12.5; the pre-spring difference is called not significant).
W6  not found      The passages say exact integer-programming methods exist and were run; none compares the simple points count with them for the title.
W7  found in part  Fixed phase and every second or third obliquity cycle are stated, but chance is rejected at 5%, not at about 1% or better.
W8  found          Graham-Squire and McCune: almost always the Condorcet winner, one failure (Burlington), one election without a Condorcet winner; "one" lies in "one or two".
W9  found          Keller and Vosshall state both halves: sulfur biased toward unpleasant, and correlated with "garlic".
W10 found          Musch and Hay state the effect across countries with different cut-off dates and the shifted peak after Australia's 1989 change.
W11 found in part  The blog gives win rates by odds band (100, 0, 75, 67 on 5, 2, 4, 6 battles) and says the pattern is not clear; the claim's pooled figure is not stated, only derivable, and nothing is quoted for the larger side winning 60%.
W12 not found      No quoted passage states face-up/corner-up/never-edge or the 0.23-0.77 range; Anderson only cites a paper not read, and Physics Today says the stable orientations over a wide range exclude corner-up, which contradicts the claim's middle.
W13 found          Burton et al. give the critical aspect ratio 0.75 for ice in seawater, the claim's number.
W14 found          Hauert and Doebeli state that spatial structure reduces cooperators for a wide range of parameters (intermediate and high r).
W15 found in part  The source states listing order and a spike in the ten-minute bin 16:00-16:10; a pile-up in the first seconds or minute is a finer claim than a ten-minute bin shows.
W16 found in part  Jiang et al. state the fitter eventually leads and that competitions can be very long (power-law tails), without the thousand-sales odds or an astronomical figure.
